s and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":28},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":10,"html":11,"skills":12,"hooks":13,"files":14,"sources":21},"read-guard","mod","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[6,7,8,9],"read","context","tokens","guard","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Stops a single \u003Ccode>Read\u003C/code> of a large file from filling your context. When Claude reads a big file with no \u003Ccode>offset\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>limit\u003C/code>, the read is capped to the first 400 lines and Claude gets a note telling it to find the part it needs and read that range.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>You work in repos with large generated files, lockfiles, long modules or logs.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>You see Claude read whole files when it needed one function.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Applies only to \u003Ccode>Read\u003C/code> calls with no \u003Ccode>offset\u003C/code> and no \u003Ccode>limit\u003C/code>. An explicit range always passes.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Files at or under the size limit (40 KB by default) pass untouched.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Images, PDFs, SVGs and notebooks pass untouched.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A capped read returns the first lines plus a note with the file size and how to read the rest.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Configuration\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Set these with \u003Ccode>/config\u003C/code>, or under \u003Ccode>pluginConfigs\u003C/code> in your user settings.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>maxBytes\u003C/code> (default \u003Ccode>40000\u003C/code>): files larger than this get capped.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>capLines\u003C/code> (default \u003Ccode>400\u003C/code>): how many lines a capped read returns.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Claude Code 2.1.287 or later.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[],[],[15,16,17,18,19,20],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","hooks/hooks.json","hooks/register.test.ts","hooks/register.ts","tsconfig.json",[22,24,26],{"path":17,"html":23},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"modules\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"./register.ts\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>",{"path":19,"html":25},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">import\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> type\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { Register } \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">from\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 'claude-code'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">const\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> BINARY\u003C/